+// SSL_set_tls13_cipher_prefs configures `ssl` to advertise, in the ClientHello,
+// the TLS 1.3 cipher suites named in `str` in exactly the order they appear
+// there, overriding the default ordering that depends on AES hardware support.
+// `str` uses the same ':'-separated cipher-name syntax as
+// `SSL_set_strict_cipher_list`; tokens that do not name a TLS 1.3 cipher suite
+// (TLS 1.2 cipher names, rule keywords, etc.) are ignored, so the exact same
+// string passed to `SSL_set_strict_cipher_list` may be reused here. A null or
+// empty string, or one naming no TLS 1.3 cipher, clears the override and
+// restores the default behavior. It returns one on success and zero on failure.
+//
+// Note: unlike `SSL_set_strict_cipher_list`, which only controls TLS 1.2 and
+// below, this function is the only way to influence TLS 1.3 cipher ordering,
+// which is otherwise fixed.
+OPENSSL_EXPORT int SSL_set_tls13_cipher_prefs(SSL *ssl, const char *str);
